{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.GaugeAnsatzNesting","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.GaugeAnsatzNesting","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Prod","lean:module:QOU.Shared.ZPowFinsetProd","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Defs"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.isCoboundary_torus_of_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.isCoboundary_torus_of_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaugeAnsatzNesting.lean#L121-L140","doc":"**The instance the probe measures.**  The two `PGL(3)`-torus columns of a cusp sum to\nthat cusp's scalar column, i.e. `φ` forgets the diagonal level (`Bool`) and keeps the cusp.\nMeasured `128/128` exactly over `ℤ` in\n`computations/ptolemy/ptolemy_gauge_ansatz_nesting.py`.\n\nBinders are restated rather than inherited: the section's `[Fintype J]` does not by itself\ngive `Fintype (Bool × L)` at the instantiation `J := Bool × L`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.strictly_stronger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.strictly_stronger","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaugeAnsatzNesting.lean#L113-L119","doc":"**#7092 asks the strictly stronger question.**  Under the fibre-sum relation the coarse\n(scalar) question implies the fine (torus) one, so a coarse negative is consistent with a\nfine positive and is not evidence against it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.isCoboundary_fine_of_coarse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.isCoboundary_fine_of_coarse","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaugeAnsatzNesting.lean#L101-L111","doc":"**The chain.**  If every coarse row is the corresponding fine row summed over the fibres\nof `φ`, then a coarse coboundary is a fine coboundary.  Contrapositively a fine *no* forces\na coarse *no*, so (fine yes, coarse no) is the only informative pattern and (fine no, coarse\nyes) is impossible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IsCoboundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IsCoboundary","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaugeAnsatzNesting.lean#L95-L99","doc":"**The form the coboundary question is asked in.**  `IsCoboundary A r` says the observed\nratio `r`, one value per coordinate, is `∏_c z c ^ A c` for some gauge `z` — simultaneously\nfor every coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.gaugeVal_comp_of_fiberSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.gaugeVal_comp_of_fiberSum","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaugeAnsatzNesting.lean#L72-L93","doc":"**A coarse row is a fine row summed over the fibres of `φ`.**  Then the coarse gauge\nvalue of `lam` is the fine gauge value of `lam ∘ φ` — the coarse ansatz is the fine one\nrestricted to assignments constant on each fibre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.gaugeVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.gaugeVal","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/GaugeAnsatzNesting.lean#L68-L70","doc":"The gauge value of one exponent row `A` under an assignment `z` of scalars to columns:\n`∏_c z c ^ A c`. Integer exponents, so this is a `zpow` product in a `CommGroup`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}